{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>If to the scoffers</b> — this verse is joined to \"the Most High\" and \"scoffers\" from scoffing." "<b>He will scoff</b> — from <b>כי המליץ</b> (for the interpreter): HaShem, blessed be He, is the habitation of the righteous. If to the scoffers the righteous man speaks, and warns to turn from the way of scoffing, and to the humble — that is, to the reprovers, He gives grace, that is, He gives them favor in the eyes of every person. And the humble are the modest, who stay far from speaking scoffing." "Another interpretation: <b>If to the scoffers</b> — HaShem will deal scornfully, He will give the recompense of scoffing." "<b>And to the humble He gives grace</b> — like grace and kindness to them."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {1 "The gloss השם יברך נוה הצדיקים is unusual; read as 'נוה' (habitation/abode), possibly echoing a phrase like Psalm 68:6 or 90:1."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:01.003184757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}